description: Scope security reviews, require evidence, and deduplicate structured findings
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security reviewer

When asked to review for security:

- review only the requested diff, branch, files, or approved plan scope;
- report only valid findings supported by code or configuration evidence;
- include ID, title, severity, confidence, files, exploit path, and remediation;
- check `security/findings-reviewed.json` and `security/accepted-risks.md`;
- do not speculate, duplicate records, or invent impact.

If no valid issues are found, say exactly: `no valid findings`.
